+# Managed GSVA scatter-page candidate and c064 terminal assessment
+
+The private source candidate changes managed direct-home GSVA CPU translation
+from the first physical address plus offset to an explicit backing-TID S1
+page-table walk. Each page is resolved independently. Failed translation,
+invalid page geometry, partial route pages, and overflowing route/window
+arithmetic are rejected. Coherence, retired-segment and stale-TLB checks remain
+in place; valid legacy contiguous cache routes retain their window behavior.
+
+`patches/gsva-scatter-home-v1/qemu.patch` applies to the QEMU commit recorded in
+`profiles/mem-service-gsva-scatter-home-v1.json`. The profile binds all three
+before/after source hashes and the patch hash. It describes a source and HOST
+object candidate. It grants no runtime replacement, Guest boot, allocation,
+ledger mutation or release authority. The separated-pages kernel profile and
+all existing runtime binaries remain unchanged.
+
+## Validation
+
+`uflow_gsva_scatter_host.py` checks the external profile digest and all source
+pins, extracts the two actual candidate C functions, and compiles them inside
+`tests/fixtures/gsva_scatter_harness.c`. Boundary mocks use named synthetic
+mapping tables and byte arrays. They never access Guest/device/kernel memory.
+The fixture tests contiguous and noncontiguous pages, cross-page reads/writes,
+backing TID selection, denied translation with no failed-page buffer access,
+range/page/overflow errors, coherence errors, and valid legacy behavior.
+These tests do not promise atomic rollback of a multi-page operation.
+
+The default compiler options request ASan and UBSan. A caller can explicitly
+select `--sanitizers none`; the result records the actual selection. In the
+current B environment the first sanitizer link failed because `libasan` and
+`libubsan` are unavailable. The original failure is retained. The explicit
+unsanitized run passed with `-Wall -Wextra -Werror` and stack protection;
+sanitizer execution is **not** claimed. Separately, both complete modified
+translation units compiled using the existing official build's compile
+database, with object/dependency outputs redirected into the new task prefix.
+The subsequent private release reproduces the fixed ELF with an unchanged
+control link, then links a separate corrected ELF. No real Guest validation
+has been performed.
+
+## Current c064 responsibility
+
+`uflow_c064_platform.py` binds the exact c064 state, actual owner capture,
+original serial and supplemental physical metadata report. The old c044 state
+and caller readiness flags are rejected. The existing publication/journal
+assessment remains `INCOMPLETE`: the original nodeA complete journal is absent.
+
+The initial assessment-only `evaluate_terminal_v2(request_path, external_sha256)`
+API and `--terminal-v2` CLI in this original module assess a different
+terminal-domain predicate. Actual
+anonymous RAM/owner context observations are reported with their source-derived
+environment basis explicitly identified. A complete current allocator,
+kernel/agent/worker, lower-record and FM confinement source graph, and an
+independently validated terminal classification of all retained carrier
+metadata, are not supplied. This implementation returns typed `INCOMPLETE`
+with zero eligible capacity. It cannot issue a release permit. The missing
+journal is preserved as a fact, without making it the v2 rejection rule.
+
+The original assessment-only v2 request contains only `schema`, the existing envelope `interface`,
+`kind=c064-terminal-private-cpu-domain-v2-request`, and four external references
+`state`, `capture`, `serial`, `physical`; each reference has an absolute path,
+size and SHA-256. The returned assessment has its own distinct v2 interface and
+a canonical `assessment_sha256` over the remaining fields. It never asserts
+normal metadata publication, native/SDK ACK, fences, ledger changes, payload
+destruction or new allocation authority. All original history and retained
+files remain unchanged. A future complete producer requires independent
+review and corresponding consumer validation before a real transaction.
+
+In the current execution, five Python contract tests passed, and repeated
+fresh v2 assessments and the actual v2 CLI agreed on `INCOMPLETE`, zero eligible
+capacity. Both command exit receipts are zero. The unchanged E0 final task-disk
+audit then exceeded its bound, so the whole job still has actual exit 1 with
+its process tree and task resources closed. The original failed whole-job
+receipt is retained. Neither the guard nor its 8-second/300,000-entry limits
+were changed, and no standalone whole-root diagnostic or retry was attempted.
+
+Current actual pool destruction remains unproven. Physical process/endpoint
+closure is distinct from logical responsibility closure. No accounting change,
+new pool, Guest, allocation, or FM payload deletion is performed by these tools.
+
+## Complete private release and current terminal producer
+
+The next source revision adds `uflow_qemu_profile.py` and the separate
+`uflow_terminal_domain_v2.py`. The latter is the complete source-bound current
+producer, superseding the assessment-only API for this particular purpose.
+The initial assessment, all failed jobs and all original runtime evidence
+remain unchanged. See `uflow-qemu-private-release.md` for the producer contract,
+source/ELF binding, real checks, and consumer boundary.
