@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@
+# Corrected-QEMU metadata and retained union
+
+This is a new HOST observation interface. The accepted old metadata, evidence,
+fixed-launch, terminal, QEMU profile and releases keep their original bytes.
+It does not launch QEMU, consume a terminal candidate, change an accounting
+record, prove an SDK drain ACK, or remove any FM file.
+
+`uflow_profile_metadata_v2.py` freshly executes three byte-pinned dependencies
+from its own directory, after checking all three: evidence 0dc9, metadata 3edf,
+and the actual QEMU profile producer e295. Its production closure is these
+four Python files. Consumers must hash the whole closure against the reviewed
+release manifest before loading the new module; do not select arbitrary Python
+via a request or reuse a cached module. Dependency functions are reused without
+changing old FIXED/SOURCE_SHA constants. All new data uses schema 2 and interface
+`mem-service-profile-metadata-v2`.
+
+## External review and actual run case
+
+Manager/C review the actual runtime package and **actual final case digest**.
+A digest binds data; possession of a digest does not grant execution or ledger
+authority. This release deliberately contains no future C source commit, PID,
+Guest boot, handle or production case. No HOST fixture is a production anchor.
+The case is a JSON object with:
+
+- `schema:2`, `interface`, `kind:"captured-runtime-case-v2"`,
+  `evidence_mode:"captured-runtime"`, `run_path:R/runs/cNNN` (new, after c068).
+- `profile_manifest_sha256:eb667be...`, `writer_source_sha256:42c93476...`.
+- `runtime_sources`: exact roles `collector`, `matrix`, `metadata_consumer`,
+  `profile_gate`, `source_manifest`, `launch_config`, `group`, `E0_runner`.
+  Each reference is `{path,bytes,sha256}`. The first six are real reviewed
+  task-implementation inputs, not empty placeholders. Group 05c2 and E0 c1b7
+  remain frozen. The source-manifest's package closure and the collector's
+  semantics are reviewed by manager/C; E hashes these accepted source inputs.
+- `registry_directory:P/registry/cNNN`, where
+  `P=R/implementation/c064-profile-metadata-v1`.
+- `artifacts`: exact roles `starts`, `identities`, `capture`, `control`,
+  `carriers`, `endpoints`, `result`, `ownership`, referring respectively to
+  `guest-starts.json`, `guest-identities.json`, `own-qemu-metadata.json`,
+  `pool-events.jsonl`, `fm-carrier-active.json`, `control-endpoints-active.json`,
+  `result.json`, `monitor/ownership-history.json` **in that exact run**.
+
+`launch_config` must select the actual release ELF and output run, with exactly
+nodeA/nodeB and their real memory sizes. Capture uses C's inline collector
+output, including producer result (its real nested source/object/link closure),
+external validator and profile manifest provenance. Each node must have its
+exact start/birth/parent, actual executable, same namespace and task UID FD
+inventory, visible anonymous RAM VMA, and explicit source-derived environment.
+The collector must actually validate `/proc` argv and process UID while alive,
+as the reviewed collector contract does. Captured metadata cannot authenticate
+itself against a hostile root; trust is the controlled E0 execution and reviewed
+collector/runtime package. No retrospective environment observation is claimed.
+
+## Registration
+
+`validate_registration(request_path,external_sha,helper_path)` returns
+`validated-profile-metadata-v2`. Requests have:
+
+- `schema`, `interface`, `kind:"metadata-registration-request-v2"`, `case`
+  (reviewed case reference), `run`, `fm_root`, `metadata_kind` bootstrap/retired.
+- `file_identity`: exact path, dev, inode, uid, file_type, bytes, mtime_ns,
+  content_sha256 and kernel_inode_aliases.
+- `qemu_binary_sha256:3c34d92d...`, `writer_source_sha256:42c93476...`.
+- `control_log`, zero-based `control_line`, `guest_node`, `guest_boot_id`,
+  `guest_incarnation`, `qemu_owner:{pid,birth}`.
+- `qemu_log`, zero-based `qemu_line`, `worker_stdout`, `journal_summary`, and
+  **both** `journal_captures:{nodeA:...,nodeB:...}`.
+
+Journal capture references use the unchanged `captured-serial-v1` format:
+`{format,source:{path,bytes,sha256},bytes,sha256}` where outer bytes/hash describe
+the reconstructed bounded journal. Summary has `journals` with both node rows,
+each containing capture_end, bytes, sha256, and independently decoded frames.
+Both serial sources must have unique complete BEGIN/CHUNK/END framing and FNV,
+and every 1024-byte frame has its own sequence and FNV. A matching published
+frame, actual worker stdout and successful QEMU publication/retirement event
+are required. Descriptor parsing reads only allowed integer slices and never
+offset 92/token_value. Retired metadata remains a QEMU observation, not SDK ACK.
+
+The actual profile producer revalidates the ELF, ordered link closure, all 1768
+inputs, source and object identities. Six actual publication/path/retirement
+functions must be lexically identical in cf803 and 42c93476; strings/comments
+are parsed when extracting definitions. The old executable identity is never
+substituted into a new request.
+
+`append_registration(directory,expected_head,entry)` revalidates the entry,
+serializes writers with a nonblocking scoped lock, verifies the entire chain,
+and publishes a new immutable numbered JSON with atomic no-replace linking
+and fsync. Heads start at 64 zeroes. Exact repeated entries are idempotent;
+conflicting paths/events or stale heads fail. `registry_history(directory,head)`
+revalidates every request, not just caller-supplied booleans. A torn extra file
+is a failure; never delete/repair it silently. The old registry is never written.
+
+## Exact closed union
+
+`validate_closed_union(plan_path,external_sha)` (also `companion_audit`) accepts
+`schema:2`, `interface`, `kind:"closed-union-plan-v2"`, `helper_path`,
+`historical_candidate_sha256:57df8009...`, `historical_consumption_receipt`
+(actual independently reviewed C transaction receipt reference), `cases`
+(nonempty complete list of reviewed case references), and
+`registry_heads:{cNNN:head,...}` with exactly the listed runs.
+
+Historical 62 = old 50 carriers + genuine old normal registration + c064 ten
+prebusiness carriers + c064 163-byte quarantined marker. Its immutable evidence
+is derived from accepted candidate 57df/source graph 12c/original physical input
+f3e0 and pinned by canonical inventory 56d8276f (including all 117 birth pairs,
+controls, aliases and file rows). No terminal evaluator is called. The original
+marker remains uncertain publication, never normal-registered; the old normal
+entry is revalidated through its genuine old request. Only the marker's nine
+allowed integer metadata fields and genuine normal metadata are read. Other
+FM payload/transport/discovery contents are never read.
+
+Each new run adds its reviewed prebusiness ten carriers, constrained to the
+same exact flat source-defined names/types/geometry, and **all** fresh normal
+bootstrap/retired entries in its new registry. Missing files, replacement,
+unknown extra, directory alias, unexpected ownership, hardlink or kernel alias
+change fail. Only these named FM roots are enumerated (8192 entries/15s).
+All historical and new monitor/ownership births must be gone; controls must be
+inactive in the bounded kernel Unix table; the unchanged frozen helper scans
+exact inode aliases for FD/VMA holders or denied visibility. No full-R audit.
+
+Output `PASS_READONLY_CLOSED_UNION_ONLY` proves this physical/file audit only.
+It includes the reviewed consumption receipt as a reference. C/manager verify
+that receipt's actual ledger semantics; E reports
+`historical_accounting_semantics_verified_by_E:false`, does not replay release,
+and never derives current service balance from old B128/A128 observations.
+Normal SDK ACK, accounting/fences and matrix success remain separate gates.
+
+## C integration points and HOST limits
+
+In `pool_run_metadata.complete_run`, replace old 56fa/cf803 construction with
+the new case and request schema. Do not call old `verify_publication` with
+fake legacy values. Use new `validate_registration` for event-candidate
+selection, new append and exact final plan; check both journals before first
+append. Populate the case from the reviewed **actual** launch/runtime and
+inline collector, with its real profile provenance. After real run closure,
+pin the full case/plan and all registry heads; call the new union audit with
+the actual C consumption receipt and all retained new runs. Keep existing
+matrix/SDK/ledger gates active.
+
+`validate_fixture_registration` and `validate_fixture_union` are separate HOST
+interfaces restricted to P/fixtures/cNNN, fixture case/request/plan kinds and
+HOST_fixture_only outputs. They use the same profile/event/journal/union code
+but synthesized captures. Production registration/append reject their outputs.
+Tests demonstrate actual profile/writer selection, synthetic bootstrap/retired
+bindings and 62+10+2=74 exact union with real helper FD/VMA negatives. They do
+not claim real corrected-QEMU Guest publication, retirement, matrix pass,
+accounting consumption or final production shutdown. Those are NOT-RUN here.
