index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2641af3fef3a5ded766af55e78b66e8aec70fb95
--- /dev/null
+++ b/guest-linux/aarch64/docs/uflow-qemu-domain.md
@@ -0,0 +1,231 @@
+# Private CPU-QEMU host evidence
+
+The `mem-service-private-qemu-domain-v1` tools register source-defined export
+metadata and assess a terminal CPU-emulation domain-loss candidate. They never
+perform a ledger transaction, release an allocation, delete FM carriers or start
+a Guest. The exact public interface is in the adjacent profile JSON.
+
+The current c044 assessment is separate from its original failing runtime and
+physical-audit results. A passing companion audit means the exact registered
+file union has no known live owner or FD/VMA holder and its controls are inactive.
+It does not prove the original SDK acknowledged release. Original Unknown and
+Mapped history remains intact.
+
+## Reviewed inputs and loading
+
+All public producers take an absolute manifest path plus an independently
+reviewed SHA-256. Nested evidence references contain `path`, `bytes`, `sha256`.
+Inputs must be stable ordinary files; symlinks, FIFOs, oversized, truncated,
+duplicate-key and nonfinite JSON inputs are rejected. The general reader refuses
+FM contents. Only the metadata validator can read the two bounded metadata
+schemas, after checking the exact identity, path, owner and publication binding.
+
+Consumers must verify the delivered hashes of **all four Python modules** before
+executing them. A preexisting module or `.pyc` cache is not an authority. For
+example, in a fresh trusted Python process, load the verified source bytes:
+
+```python
+import hashlib, sys, types
+from pathlib import Path
+
+# pins comes from the independently reviewed delivery manifest, never its own
+# unreviewed contents. Verify every module before executing any of them.
+names = ("uflow_qemu_evidence", "uflow_qemu_metadata",
+         "uflow_qemu_fixed_launch", "uflow_qemu_domain")
+bodies = {}
+for name in names:
+    path = Path(reviewed_directory) / (name + ".py")
+    bodies[name] = path.read_bytes()
+    assert hashlib.sha256(bodies[name]).hexdigest() == pins[name + ".py"]
+assert not any(name in sys.modules for name in names)
+for name in names:
+    module = types.ModuleType(name)
+    module.__file__ = str(Path(reviewed_directory) / (name + ".py"))
+    sys.modules[name] = module
+    exec(compile(bodies[name], module.__file__, "exec"), module.__dict__)
+validator = sys.modules["uflow_qemu_domain"].validate_candidate
+candidate = validator(candidate_path, reviewed_candidate_sha256)
+```
+
+## Metadata registration
+
+`uflow_qemu_metadata.validate_registration(request_path, reviewed_sha, helper)`
+returns a validated registration. A schema-1 manifest uses
+`kind=metadata-registration-request-v1`, `interface` equal to the fixed interface,
+and these groups:
+
+* `run`, `fm_root`, `metadata_kind`, and `file_identity`: exact absolute path,
+  dev/inode/uid/type/size/mtime, content SHA and kernel inode aliases.
+* `qemu_commit`, binary and writer-source pins, `writer_source`, and all five
+  `fixed_bindings` for QEMU, Image, group, original physical helper and E0 runner.
+* Original `guest_starts`, `guest_identities`, selected node/boot/incarnation and
+  QEMU PID/birth; original control log and zero-based successful publication
+  line; exact QEMU event log and line; worker publication stdout.
+* `journal_summary` and `journal_capture`: the latter is either a bounded binary
+  **metadata fixture** or a `captured-serial-v1` record with the original serial
+  reference plus decoded-journal byte count and hash. Serial chunks, full capture
+  FNV, frame ABI, sequence, frame FNV, hashes and allowed identity fields are
+  independently verified in memory. Original opaque bytes are not copied out.
+
+Bootstrap files contain a single `[obmm_export]` section and exactly the nine
+unsigned integer keys in the interface. Retired files contain exactly six keys,
+with no section. Basenames must encode the observed identity. Temporary files
+cannot enter the registry. The initial implementation admits zero bootstrap
+flags only; a new flag route needs explicit source/descriptor evidence support.
+
+Only the descriptor's documented export identity slices are decoded. Its
+`token_value` field is never decoded or returned. The complete opaque descriptor
+is bound by a digest. A retired observation is not a native close receipt.
+
+`append_registration(new_directory, previous_head, validated_entry)` creates
+numbered immutable JSON records with previous-record hashes. Publication uses a
+no-replace hard link and directory fsync. Exact retries are idempotent; stale new
+appends, conflicts, gaps, duplicates, torn temporary records and changed entries
+fail. Writes inside the current task root are restricted to the new private
+implementation directory; original registries cannot be extended by this tool.
+Companion audits revalidate every entry, including its evidence and actual file.
+
+The CLI supports `register` and `audit`, with `--manifest`,
+`--manifest-sha256`, and a new `--output`. Registration also requires `--helper`,
+`--registry`, `--previous-head`. Outputs never overwrite an existing artifact.
+
+## Companion audit
+
+`companion_audit(plan_path, reviewed_sha)` takes a schema-1
+`readonly-companion-plan-v1` manifest: `original_carriers` reference,
+`registry_directory`, pinned `registry_head_sha256`, `helper_path`, exact
+PID-to-birth `births`, and `control_endpoints` identity records.
+
+It loads the exact frozen physical helper source and calls its actual identity,
+inode-alias and holder primitives. It does not call the old full audit, acquire
+the production or Guest lock, unlink a control socket, or rewrite an old audit.
+The original carrier set and validated dynamic metadata form an exact union.
+Unknown extras, changed aliases/uid/inode/type/size, live births, held FD/VMA,
+active or replaced sockets and incomplete proc visibility reject the audit.
+Original already-absent files retain that observation; disappearing dynamic
+metadata is rejected. Enumeration has an 8192-entry/15-second bound; original
+holder primitives retain their 6000-process, million-FD, 15-second limits.
+
+`quarantine_metadata_observation(path, fm_root)` records only a named temporary
+file's stat identity. It returns INCOMPLETE and never admits that file to a union.
+
+## Domain candidate
+
+`uflow_qemu_domain.produce(plan_path, reviewed_sha)` takes a schema-1
+`cpu-qemu-domain-request-v1` manifest. It binds `fixed_bindings`, `source_graph`,
+the exact current `state`, `guest_starts`, `guest_identities`, historical Guest
+and monitor configs, plus a reviewed `companion_plan`. The `captured-runtime`
+method also
+requires `runtime_observations`, `backing_observations`, `owner_observations`:
+
+* Runtime observations identify both original PID/birth/argv contexts, loaded
+  binary, UID, host boot and namespaces, effective selected environment,
+  original Guest boot, and referenced proc/QMP captures. Captures must show CPU
+  emulation, private anonymous machine RAM, exact RAM geometry, no file/memfd
+  backing and no unexplained management/migration/snapshot/save endpoint.
+* Backing observations close all three current resources over both owning Guest
+  RAM contexts, bind their source/provider/session identities, and exclude any
+  external native backing or saved state. Owner observations bind both QEMU
+  contexts and every original client; no external native owner may be omitted.
+
+Typed evidence is a reviewed evidence graph, not a caller `ready=true` flag.
+Immutable historical captures must have independent provenance. A dead process
+cannot be queried retrospectively. Current defaults or a newly started Guest
+cannot reconstruct the original historical environment and backing proof.
+
+The only eligible scope is resource IDs 110/111/112, at most 52 MiB. The old
+12 MiB retained obligations and 64 MiB CreationUnknown reservation are protected.
+The actual current state path and hash are mandatory; a copied snapshot is not
+current authority. Missing evidence returns INCOMPLETE with zero current
+eligibility and precise evidence recovery limits. A `synthetic-fixture` can pass
+the predicate but always has `applies_to_current_domain=false` and zero current
+eligibility. It cannot be consumed as the current c044 domain.
+
+`validate_candidate(path, reviewed_candidate_sha, for_current_domain=True)`
+reproduces the assessment from fresh pinned inputs and a fresh physical audit.
+Changed state, sources, registry, closure or manifest invalidate the candidate.
+Exact repeated validation is read-only and idempotent. One-time consumption,
+permanent anti-revival fences, crash recovery and ledger succession belong to
+the later C transaction, and are explicitly absent here.
+
+The domain CLI takes `--manifest`, `--manifest-sha256`, `--output`. Exit 0 is a
+HOST candidate; exit 3 writes a truthful INCOMPLETE assessment; exit 2 rejects an
+invalid request. All authority and native-ACK truth fields remain false as
+specified by the interface.
+
+## Independent fixed launch method
+
+`evidence_mode=fixed-launch-source` adds a separate c044-only inference. It keeps
+the original captured-runtime checks and old INCOMPLETE results. Its manifest
+adds `fixed_launch`, a referenced `fixed-launch-source-c044-v1` document with
+`trust_model=reviewed-E0-controlled-normal-execution` and the exact evidence
+references consumed by `uflow_qemu_fixed_launch.validate`.
+
+This method uses the accepted launcher's controlled normal execution model. It
+does not claim forensic resistance to hostile root, a modified kernel, arbitrary
+injection or timestamp tampering. It cannot be generalized to an unknown run,
+hardware/NPU, the old retained 12 MiB or CreationUnknown 64 MiB.
+
+The validator checks seven independently pinned primary source/metadata/transport
+records, six additional fixed QEMU source files, the exact generated build
+header, original E0/monitor/group configuration, supervisor source, complete
+original HOST034 source/build/SDK/agent/official-worker closure, exact topology
+and entity plan, actual QEMU argv and full task/client owners. It binds the real
+publication descriptor/journal and both original canaries to their Guest boots.
+The fresh exact 51-file physical companion audit remains mandatory.
+
+`-nodefaults` does **not** disable default qemu.conf loading. The pinned relocation
+source and actual executable/build header derive the real configuration path as
+`executable-directory/qemu-bundle/usr/local/etc/qemu/qemu.conf`. The real root
+bundle must be readable, and that file, its qemu directory and its etc directory
+must be absent. Their first existing ancestor's dev/inode/UID/type/mode/mtime/ctime
+must match independently recorded metadata and predate the original config's
+prestart ctime. Executable/bundle/config-header/config identities also must remain
+stable. Merely observing an absent file now is insufficient. Replacement,
+symlinks, late ctime or a config that appears later reject the inference.
+
+The original sealed SSH/Docker argv must match exactly, with no `-e`, environment
+or shell entrypoint override. The original immutable container ID/create/start
+record must predate launch and contain no LD_PRELOAD/LD_AUDIT/QEMU_RAM_PATH keys;
+no values or other environment are read. Original config env and command env are
+checked exactly. The pinned matrix/group/supervisor sources establish subsequent
+environment overrides and the QMP lifecycle whitelist. The daemon-specific fence
+library is not treated as a QEMU preload.
+
+With no configuration/argv RAM override, the fixed source chain establishes
+memory-backend-ram, own Guest RAMBlock/address_space, fd=-1 anonymous/private mmap
+and process-local OBMM exports. Guest kernel/user backing and all clients remain
+inside the two proved owning contexts; the fixed two-node FM topology is only
+their simulated transport. Its files remain retained. The result explicitly
+sets `source_derived_inference=true`,
+`historical_proc_or_QMP_capture_claimed=false`, and carries the inference graph.
+It never invents old proc/QMP observations, native ACK or ledger fences.
+
+CPU-only selection also requires the actual build's TCG enabled/modules disabled
+configuration and defined TCG class/ops registration symbols parsed from the
+fixed ELF. Pinned `system/vl.c` selects this built-in TCG first for the actual
+non-kvm executable name. Both complete original stdout/stderr logs are streamed
+under their independently reviewed byte counts/hashes and accelerator-start
+prefix; any TCG initialization failure, invalid accelerator or fallback rejects
+the inference. Absence of an `-accel` flag alone is insufficient.
+
+The complete predicate may yield `PASS_HOST_CANDIDATE_ONLY` and current 52 MiB
+eligibility for this fixed run. Eligibility still grants no transaction or
+refund. One-time permanent fencing and durable succession remain C's separate
+responsibility after independent review. A synthetic fixture can select this
+method with `evidence_method=fixed-launch-source`, but always has zero current
+eligibility and is rejected by normal current-domain consumption.
+
+## Linux validation
+
+Run only on the authorized HOST test target under its finite supervisor. Set
+`UFLOW_QEMU_DOMAIN_BASE_PLAN` to the reviewed current domain manifest,
+`UFLOW_QEMU_DOMAIN_TEST_ROOT` to a new private fixture directory and
+`UFLOW_QEMU_DOMAIN_TEST_SOCKET` to a fresh short socket pathname inside the
+private task scope. Also set `UFLOW_QEMU_DOMAIN_FIXED_PLAN` to the reviewed fixed
+launch manifest to exercise its full positive and negative predicates without
+skips. Run `tests/test_uflow_qemu_domain.py`. It starts only bounded
+Python fixture children, including a genuine VMA-only holder with no FD, and
+reaps them. No Guest, QEMU, KVM, NPU or business pool is started. The proc-denied
+negative is explicitly a fault-injection unit test; real visibility is checked
+separately by the unmodified helper in actual audits.
