+# Private corrected QEMU and the c064 terminal witness
+
+The corrected executable is a separate HOST candidate. The original QEMU
+`56fab4e5…`, kernel Image `95165fea…`, original c064 captures, state and FM files
+remain unchanged. No QEMU process or Guest was started for these checks.
+
+## Executable identity
+
+The original wrapper-generated Ninja link recipe names the two affected
+objects directly. A control link using its original inputs reproduced every
+byte of the fixed QEMU executable. The candidate link used the same ordered
+inputs and flags, replacing only the two previously compiled candidate
+objects. All 1,768 reused input identities, including the members of 18 thin
+archives, were rechecked. Original archives and objects were not rewritten.
+The header delta adds one function prototype; existing declarations and type
+layouts remain unchanged. The ELF contains both actual candidate functions.
+
+`uflow_qemu_profile.validate(manifest_path, external_manifest_sha256,
+qemu_binary_path)` verifies the externally pinned manifest, selected ordinary
+executable, original/control/candidate byte identities, exact three-file
+source delta and patch, actual compiler/object receipts, ordered link input
+substitutions, reused input hashes, thin archive membership and toolchain
+identities. Its result is `mem-service-private-qemu-profile-v1`, profile
+`mem-service-gsva-scatter-home-v1`, `PASS_HOST_QEMU_PROFILE_ONLY`.
+`runtime_tested` and `authority_to_boot_or_replace_existing_binary` are false.
+
+Eight actual HOST tests cover the valid release and rejection of a wrong
+external pin, old executable selection, changed source hash, false runtime
+claim, wrong control identity, changed linker flag and omitted thin-archive
+member. Actual CLI validation also runs against the published release files.
+Earlier failures involving a system-library symlink and a legitimate empty
+`block.syms` response file remain as original failed job evidence.
+
+## Current terminal-domain predicate
+
+`profiles/mem-service-terminal-c064-v2.json` binds the reviewed source graph:
+current launch/build receipts and source, Guest allocator/agent/worker,
+kernel/UMMU, original QEMU/route/private-RAM paths, lower metadata handling,
+and FM transport/metadata writers. The producer hardcodes the graph digest,
+original evidence digests, current state digest and exact current paths.
+It also verifies all 239 files/modes in the actual HOST047 source snapshot,
+the inherited HOST046 image/source closure, 233 official-worker source/link
+inputs, SDK53 and the real accepted kernel producer. The private corrected
+ELF is not substituted into this historical proof.
+
+`uflow_terminal_domain_v2.evaluate_terminal_v2(request_path,
+external_request_sha256)` checks the distinct terminal-private-CPU-domain
+predicate. The source-bound inline capture independently checked exact
+PID/birth/parent, all four UID fields, namespaces, actual argv/executable and
+FD/VMA metadata. Each original owner has one observed 2 GiB anonymous private
+RAM candidate. Selected launch environment values are explicitly a
+source-derived inference, not a historical child environment capture.
+The unchanged predecessor default-config ancestry is reused only as a
+configuration/relocation fact, never as a c044 release ticket.
+
+The producer binds the current three BackingIds, actual Guest boot identities,
+provider/session/pool tuple, successful worker descriptor metadata slices,
+original QEMU event and worker stdout. It independently validates the unique
+163-byte bootstrap marker against its exact original inode/mtime/aliases and
+nine-integer source schema. That marker is quarantined metadata with uncertain
+normal publication. It is not appended to the original v1 registry. No secret
+descriptor token value is decoded or exported.
+
+Fresh closure reconstructs the exact 62-file set: original 50 carriers,
+one previously accepted metadata file, the current 10 pre-business carriers,
+and the unique current marker. Only these named FM roots are enumerated.
+Source-defined transport files remain retained; no claim is made that residual
+packet bytes are erased. Original task/ownership histories and the current
+three clients are checked against 117 precise process births, followed by
+fresh exact-inode FD/VMA and control-endpoint checks. A read-only FD holder
+negative test opens a named ring without reading or mapping any byte; the
+producer correctly returns `INCOMPLETE` until that FD is closed.
+
+The result is a terminal-only candidate for current resources 113/114/115,
+2+2+48 MiB. Protected historical 76 MiB and prior c063 terminal/claimed
+successor references remain explicit. `validate_candidate(path,
+external_candidate_sha256)` independently reruns the real predicate and
+compares the entire canonical result. Caller completeness/force/readiness
+flags, old authority, substituted source/capture/log references and forged
+eligible rows cannot be accepted. Nine actual HOST tests cover these cases.
+
+The trust model is reviewed E0 controlled normal execution, with the recorded
+source-derived inferences stated explicitly. It is not forensic proof against
+hostile root, kernel or timestamp tampering. Missing/foreign/held evidence
+fails closed. The original nodeA journal remains incomplete. Normal metadata
+publication, native/SDK ACK, ledger changes, fences, new allocation authority
+and FM payload destruction are all false in the returned candidate.
+
+## Consumer boundary
+
+The private release manifests supply exact module/dependency raw hashes and
+modes, executable identities and evidence references. A consumer must verify
+all independently accepted module bytes before fresh execution; do not use
+cached modules or arbitrary caller Python as a trust anchor. The manager must
+first accept these producer pins. The real C transaction then independently
+revalidates the current witness under the same original exclusive authority,
+preserving old tombstones and the union of permanent fences. No producer
+result itself performs that transaction or grants a new Guest/allocation.
+
+The existing source-candidate synthetic page tests and two complete translation
+unit compilations are reused by their exact source hashes. ASan/UBSan execution
+remains unclaimed because the original link lacked the host libraries. The
+old final E0 audit failure remains a failed whole job. New HOST work resumed
+only after the manager's exact closed-cache cleanup, through unchanged normal
+E0 guards; no standalone whole-root diagnostic or guard relaxation was used.
