+# Current c081 HOST recovery interfaces
+
+These interfaces produce evidence. Dev/C must independently accept the exact
+code and data digests and enforce the original-authority transaction before
+any terminal consumption or new execution. A caller's self-hash is not an
+admission. E does not implement Catalog accounting or infer ACK from death.
+Old releases, claimed ancestors and missing journals remain immutable.
+
+The B-only root is `/workspace/uflow/runs/mem-service-shared-pool-20261108`;
+new artifacts live under `implementation/c081-recovery-v1`. Formal candidates
+are `release-v2/profile-manifest.json`, `terminal-context004/candidate.json`
+and `recovery-release-v5/accepted-context.json`. These are HOST candidates,
+awaiting concentrated manager review. The last context binds the actual new
+profile and current terminal classification. It does not grant boot authority.
+
+## Terminal and actual ownership
+
+`uflow_recovery_context_v3.evaluate(context_path, externally_accepted_sha256)`
+checks exact current state/source/build/runtime/native publication/physical
+closure. `validate_candidate(candidate_path, externally_accepted_sha256)` repeats
+that predicate and compares the complete normalized assessment. Failure returns
+INCOMPLETE with zero eligible rows. The v3 terminal result is specific to the
+recorded current c081 authority; it never replays 57df or either claimed chain.
+
+The current domain binds 64014 source276, actual compiled ed76 daemon735c48,
+69 unchanged Rust inputs and 24 include occurrences/20 unique inputs, reused
+046 image/worker233/SDK53 and actual private 3c34 launch. It preserves the
+source-derived LD_LIBRARY_PATH fence selection and explicitly labels config/
+environment inference under controlled normal execution. It does not claim
+forensic proof against hostile root, kernel or timestamp tampering.
+
+The marker is read only under the nine-integer source schema, original inode,
+mtime and kernel aliases, safe native descriptor binding, worker stdout and
+source-defined QEMU event. No token_value is decoded. Normal journal evidence
+is missing on both nodes, so this marker is quarantined. The known 319991262B
+NodeB log is streamed in bounded chunks under its exact hash and retained on B;
+its historical log-budget failure remains recorded. Future 64MiB guards stay.
+
+`uflow_monitor_ownership_v3.validate_descriptor(descriptor, run, helper_path,
+starts=None, capture=None)` accepts an exact data descriptor with schema3,
+interface `mem-service-observed-ownership-v3`, kind
+`monitor-result-ownership-v3`, run, expected_exit, monitor_result, run_result,
+monitor_config, supervisor_start, launch_config, E0_runner,
+supervisor_sources and optional_history. References contain path/bytes/sha256.
+Real frozen supervisor `result.owned_births` is primary. The separately pinned
+optional history is read only when actually emitted. c080's two precise adapter
+annotations are accepted only alongside its actual history; primary members
+still match exactly. c081/c082 history is absent and never reconstructed.
+
+## New normal metadata and complete retained union
+
+`uflow_profile_metadata_v3` exports:
+
+```python
+validate_registration(request_path, request_sha, helper_path,
+                      accepted_context_path, accepted_context_sha)
+append_registration(registry_directory, expected_head, validated_entry)
+registry_history(registry_directory, expected_head)
+validate_closed_union(plan_path, plan_sha,
+                      accepted_context_path, accepted_context_sha)
+companion_audit = validate_closed_union
+```
+
+Production run paths are new `ROOT/runs/cNNN` after c082. Normal registration
+requires both genuine complete serial journals, independent frame/FNV checks,
+descriptor/boot/incarnation/worker/event matches, actual new ELF/profile/writer,
+explicit new wrapper argv and inline exe/parent/birth/UID/ns/FD/private-RAM VMA
+capture. It requires actual result-based ownership and a real closed original
+tree. Missing journals cannot be reconstructed or replaced by physical closure.
+
+A registration request has exact schema/interface/kind, case reference, run,
+fm_root, metadata_kind, file_identity, qemu_binary_sha256,
+writer_source_sha256, control_log, control_line, guest_node, guest_boot_id,
+guest_incarnation, qemu_owner, qemu_log, qemu_line, worker_stdout,
+journal_summary and journal_captures. File identity includes original
+dev/inode/uid/type/bytes/mtime/content hash/kernel aliases. Case data has exact
+schema/interface/kind/evidence_mode/run_path/accepted_context/profile_manifest/
+writer_source_sha256/runtime_sources/registry_directory/artifacts/ownership.
+The eight runtime-source roles are collector, matrix, metadata_consumer,
+profile_gate, source_manifest, launch_config, group and E0_runner. The seven
+artifact roles are starts, identities, capture, control, carriers, endpoints,
+result and their exact named run paths; ownership is the separate tagged
+descriptor. Group is the actual accepted managed wrapper, not old05c2.
+
+Each run owns `PREFIX/registry/cNNN`. Append revalidates, locks, uses no-replace
+link publication, fsyncs and checks the complete chain/head/duplicate event.
+Both bootstrap and retired registrations are required for a completed new case.
+
+The union plan has exact schema/interface/kind/helper_path,
+historical_consumption_receipt, accepted_context, cases and registry_heads.
+It derives all old73 files and actual144 births from the accepted terminal
+classification and original sources. It checks both quarantined markers again,
+without invoking terminal eligibility after consumption. It adds all new
+case carriers and both normal metadata registrations, fresh exact named FM
+enumeration, kernel inode aliases, actual births, FD/VMA holders and inactive
+controls. C's consumption receipt is byte-bound; its accounting/fence semantics
+remain C's responsibility. E derives no current balance from a receipt.
+
+Explicit `validate_fixture_registration` and `validate_fixture_union` use
+`PREFIX/fixtures/cNNN`, distinct kinds and HOST-fixture ownership. Fixture plans
+add fixture_requests. Production registration/append reject all fixture outputs.
+They cannot normal-register the failed c081 marker or alter production history.
+
+## Consumer integration and validation limits
+
+C must pin the accepted context and source closure before loading these APIs;
+load fresh verified source, not cached modules/pyc or caller Python. Launch the
+managed group from **release-v2**, whose actual path is bound by its profile;
+the copies in recovery-release-v5 are evidence, not alternate runtime paths.
+Existing `config.kernel` remains explicit. All original budget, monitor and
+first-failure notification rules stay active. Normal close rejects live or
+uncertain grants; abnormal transport disposal does not acknowledge a grant.
+
+The actual six-pass HOST model keeps all 125829120 scalar callbacks and bytes,
+using 30720 strict4KiB fills with an8MiB cache and eviction. It tests native
+home/importer binding, invalidation/revoke/epoch/token/fill races, errors, tail
+clipping, end→managed writer→fresh grant and final zero obligations. The actual
+QDict formatter linked with frozen QEMU JSON objects passes strict codec checks
+for21 real fixture replies. These prove count/correctness/control properties;
+only a later real two-Guest full matrix can establish the unchanged120s path.
+No real new Guest, terminal transaction, pool destruction or shutdown occurred
+in this HOST package.
+
+Apply the source patch with `git -c core.autocrlf=false apply --unidiff-zero` after verifying every
+base SHA in source-closure.json. The patch has zero context and reproduces
+the exact nine-file compiled overlay, including the prior scatter fix.
+
+The proposed accepted context also binds the manager-reviewed build-host066
+static ARM64 image (5c00fbbd…,13859680B), its agent/PID1/worker/SDK/compiler-input
+acceptance record, and the exact selected image file. Both node initrd arguments
+must select it. Wrong image hashes and wrong actual launch selections reject.
+The original c081 terminal context still truthfully binds its older046 image;
+this new image is exclusively a future normal-runtime dependency.
